# RECOVERY — {{REPO_NAME}}

How to get this project back, from scratch, on any machine.

## Fast path (new Mac)

```bash
# prerequisites: git, gh (authenticated as {{GH_ACCOUNT}}), git-lfs
brew install gh git-lfs && gh auth login && git lfs install
git clone git@github.com:{{GH_ACCOUNT}}/git-sot-bootstrap.git ~/Projects/_Tooling/git-sot-bootstrap
~/Projects/_Tooling/git-sot-bootstrap/bootstrap.sh restore --repo {{REPO_NAME}}
```

`restore` clones to the registry-recorded path
(`{{LOCAL_PATH}}`), initializes submodules, and pulls LFS objects.

## Manual path (no bootstrap available)

```bash
git clone --recurse-submodules git@github.com:{{GH_ACCOUNT}}/{{REPO_NAME}}.git "{{LOCAL_PATH}}"
cd "{{LOCAL_PATH}}" && git lfs pull
```

## Fallback if GitHub is unreachable

A pull-only clone lives on the server: `{{SERVER_CLONE_PATH}}`
(`{{SERVER_USER}}@{{SERVER_HOST}}`, SSH alias `{{SSH_ALIAS}}`).
Copy it off the server; do NOT commit or push from it.

